+# Document Management API
+
+Express + TypeScript document management API with hierarchical folders, granular
+sharing and an activity log. All state is in memory and resets on restart.
+
+```ts
+import { createApp } from './src/index.js'; // also exported from './src/app.js'
+const app = createApp();                    // fresh, isolated store per call
+```
+
+`npm run build` · `npm run lint` · `npm test` · `npx tsx src/index.ts` (serves on `PORT`, default 3000)
+
+## Auth
+
+All routes except register/login/health need `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
+
+| Method | Path | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| POST | `/auth/register` (aliases `/register`, `/users`, `/signup`) | `{username, password}` → 201 `{id, username, token}` |
+| POST | `/auth/login` (aliases `/login`, `/sessions`) | → 200 `{id, username, token}` |
+| POST | `/auth/logout` | revokes the current token |
+| GET | `/auth/me`, `/me` | current user |
+| GET | `/users`, `/users/:id` | directory used for sharing |
+
+## Folders & documents
+
+| Method | Path | Required role |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| POST | `/folders` `{name, parentId?}` | `editor` on the parent |
+| GET | `/folders` · `/folders/:id` · `/folders/:id/children` · `/folders/:id/documents` | `viewer` |
+| PUT/PATCH | `/folders/:id` `{name?, parentId?}` | `editor` |
+| DELETE | `/folders/:id` | `owner` (cascades to the whole subtree) |
+| POST | `/documents` `{title, content?, folderId?}` · `/folders/:id/documents` | `editor` on the folder |
+| GET | `/documents` · `/documents/:id` | `viewer` |
+| PUT/PATCH | `/documents/:id` `{title?, content?, folderId?}` | `editor` (plus `editor` on the destination folder when moving) |
+| DELETE | `/documents/:id` | `owner` |
+
+Listings only include resources the caller can read. Each resource response carries
+the caller's effective `role` (and a `permissions` summary).
+
+## Sharing
+
+| Method | Path |
+| --- | --- |
+| POST | `/documents/:id/share`, `/folders/:id/share` — `{userId \| username, role}` |
+| POST | `/share` — `{resourceType, resourceId, userId \| username, role}` |
+| GET | `/documents/:id/shares`, `/folders/:id/shares`, `/shares` |
+| DELETE | `/documents/:id/shares/:userId`, `/folders/:id/shares/:userId` |
+
+Roles are `viewer` (read), `editor` (read, modify, share) and `owner` (full control,
+delete, role management). The creator is always the owner.
+
+**Effective permission** is the most permissive role reached through any path: direct
+ownership, a direct share, or a share on *any* ancestor folder. A document in a folder
+shared as `viewer` and shared directly as `editor` resolves to `editor`. Editors may
+share, but only owners may grant or alter `owner` access, and only owners may revoke
+someone else's grant.
+
+## Activity
+
+`GET /activity` (aliases `/activities`, `/logs`) returns entries in chronological
+order — `{id, action, userId, resourceType, resourceId, timestamp, details}` — filtered
+to what the caller performed or can still read. Filters: `action`, `resourceType`,
+`resourceId`, `userId`, `order=desc`, `limit`. Per-resource feeds live at
+`/documents/:id/activity` and `/folders/:id/activity`.
+
+Actions: `user.register`, `folder.create|update|delete`, `document.create|update|delete`,
+`share.grant`, `share.revoke`.
+
+## Status codes
+
+`200` ok · `201` created · `204` deleted · `400` invalid payload · `401` missing/bad token ·
+`403` authenticated but insufficient role · `404` unknown resource · `409` duplicate username.
